<div class="calcpad-output">
 <!-- Exercises optional parameters with default values and keyword-argument calls, for both custom functions and macros. -->
 <h1>Keyword Arguments and Optional Parameters</h1>
 <p>
  A function or macro parameter can carry a default value, written with
  <b>=</b>
  in the
  <p>parameter list. A call can then omit that argument, or name it explicitly as</p>
  <b>name = value</b>
  . Required parameters come before optional ones in a definition, and
  <p>positional arguments come before keyword arguments in a call.</p>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h2>1. Functions</h2>
 <h3>1.1 Optional parameters</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>f</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   ;
   <var>y</var>
   ;
   <var>z</var>
   )  =
   <var>x</var>
   +
   <var>y</var>
   +
   <var>z</var>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Only the required argument, so y and z take their defaults</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>r</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 2; 3 )  = 6
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Every argument positional</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>r</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 10; 100 )  = 111
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Positional first, then one keyword argument</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>r</var>
   <sub>3</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 2; 100 )  = 103
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>All keyword, in any order</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>r</var>
   <sub>4</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 10; 100 )  = 111
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>1.2 Defaults carrying units</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>w</var>
   (
   <var>L</var>
   ;
   <var>q</var>
   )  =
   <span class="dvc">
    <var>q</var>
    ·
    <var>L</var>
    <sup>2</sup>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    8
   </span>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>L</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   = 6
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Default load</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>M</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   <var>L</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   ; 5
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   6
   <i>m</i>
   ; 5
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   = 22.5
   <i>kN</i>
   <i>·</i>
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Load supplied by name</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>M</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   <var>L</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   ; 12
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   6
   <i>m</i>
   ; 12
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   = 54
   <i>kN</i>
   <i>·</i>
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>1.3 Defaults are resolved at call time</h3>
 <p>
  A default is stored as source text and evaluated in the global scope on every call,
  <p>so it follows the current value of whatever it references.</p>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>k</var>
   = 5
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>g</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   ;
   <var>m</var>
   )  =
   <var>x</var>
   ·
   <var>m</var>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>k is 5 here</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>g</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>g</var>
   ( 2;
   <var>k</var>
   )  =
   <var>g</var>
   ( 2; 5 )  = 10
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>k</var>
   = 50
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>the same call, with k now 50</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>g</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>g</var>
   ( 2;
   <var>k</var>
   )  =
   <var>g</var>
   ( 2; 50 )  = 100
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>1.4 A default may be an expression or a vector</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>h</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   ;
   <var>y</var>
   )  =
   <var>x</var>
   +
   <var>y</var>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>h</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>h</var>
   ( 1;
   <span class="o0">
    <span class="r">√</span>
    16
   </span>
   )  = 5
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>h</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>h</var>
   ( 1; 100 )  = 101
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>p</var>
   (
   <var>x</var>
   ;
   <var>v</var>
   )  =
   <var>x</var>
   ·
   <b>sum</b>
   (
   <var>v</var>
   )
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>p</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>p</var>
   ( 2;
   <span class="b0">[</span>
   2; 4; 6
   <span class="b0">]</span>
   )  = 24
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>p</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>p</var>
   ( 2;
   <span class="b0">[</span>
   1; 1
   <span class="b0">]</span>
   )  = 4
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>1.5 Nested calls</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>n</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   (
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 2; 3 ) ; 4; 3 )  = 13
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>n</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>f</var>
   (
   <var>f</var>
   ( 1; 2; 0 ) ; 0; 3 )  = 6
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h2>2. Macros</h2>
 <h3>2.1 Inline macro with defaults</h3>
 <p>Only the required argument</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>m</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   = 1 + 10 + 5 = 16
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>All positional</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>m</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   = 1 + 2 + 3 = 6
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Positional then keyword</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>m</var>
   <sub>3</sub>
   = 1 + 10 + 7 = 18
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>All keyword, in any order</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>m</var>
   <sub>4</sub>
   = 1 + 2 + 7 = 10
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>2.2 Multiline macro with a default</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   = 2.5
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Default unit</p>
 <p>Converted to the requested unit:</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   = 2500
   <i>mm</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>Unit supplied by name</p>
 <p>Converted to the requested unit:</p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>d</var>
   = 250
   <i>cm</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>2.3 An empty argument list takes every default</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>s</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   = 1 + 2 = 3
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>s</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   = 1 + 20 = 21
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>2.4 A default may contain brackets</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>t</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <b>sum</b>
   (
   <span class="b0">[</span>
   1; 2; 3
   <span class="b0">]</span>
   )  = 6
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>
    <span class="vec">⃗</span>
    v
   </var>
   <sub>x</sub>
   =
   <span class="b0">[</span>
   10; 20
   <span class="b0">]</span>
   =
   <b class="b0">[</b>
   10 20
   <b class="b0">]</b>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>t</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <b>sum</b>
   (
   <var>
    <span class="vec">⃗</span>
    v
   </var>
   <sub>x</sub>
   )  = 30
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>2.5 A macro default feeding a function default</h3>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>A</var>
   <sub>1</sub>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   <var>L</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   ; 3 · 1
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   6
   <i>m</i>
   ; 3 · 1
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   = 13.5
   <i>kN</i>
   <i>·</i>
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>A</var>
   <sub>2</sub>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   <var>L</var>
   <sub>s</sub>
   ; 8 · 1
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   =
   <var>w</var>
   <span class="b1">(</span>
   6
   <i>m</i>
   ; 8 · 1
   <span class="dvc">
    <i>kN</i>
    <span class="dvl">
    </span>
    <i>m</i>
   </span>
   <span class="b1">)</span>
   = 36
   <i>kN</i>
   <i>·</i>
   <i>m</i>
  </span>
 </p>
</div>
